C.java: public static final boolean CENSUS_FADE = false;
Comms.java:112, before the existing return:
  if (C.CENSUS_FADE && phase >= 32) return Math.max(cur, prevCensus * (64 - phase) >> 5);
  return phase < 32 ? Math.max(prevCensus, cur) : cur;
prevCensus is a per-HQ static that keeps its phase-31 value; HQ 0 zeroes the slot at phase 32, not the static. The previous count now fades out over the second half of the epoch instead of vanishing in one round, so dead carriers are still replaced but builds spread over 32 rounds. A one-line variant is CENSUS_HOLD, which returns max(prevCensus, cur) at every phase; replacements then wait for the epoch boundary.

C.java: public static final boolean CENSUS_HQ_TICK = false;
Comms.java:
  static void censusBuilt() throws GameActionException {
    int e = G.round >> 6, s = CENSUS + (e & 1);
    put(s, Math.min(65535, read(s) + 1));
    // phases 0-31: the previous epoch's slot is still intact and read as prevCensus; bump it too, so max(prev, cur) moves by one
    if (e > 0 && (G.round & 63) < 32) { int p = CENSUS + ((e - 1) & 1); put(p, Math.min(65535, read(p) + 1)); }
  }
